# RISE website — environment variables
#
# All values are optional. Copy this file to `.env.local` (git-ignored) and
# set what you need. Never commit real secrets — only this example file is
# tracked.
#
# Forms persist to Supabase when its keys are set below, and fall back to a
# local filesystem store (`data/`, git-ignored) otherwise. Notifications are
# still recorded as files instead of emails; Resend (email), Sanity (content),
# and Turnstile (spam protection) swap in later behind their seams.

# Supabase: when BOTH are set, the app uses Supabase for the submission store
# (see supabase/schema.sql for the tables and Row-Level Security). The
# service-role key bypasses RLS and must stay server-side only — never prefix
# it with NEXT_PUBLIC_ and never expose it to the browser.
# SUPABASE_URL=
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=

# Where the filesystem store writes its data (only used when Supabase is unset).
# Defaults to `./data`.
# RISE_DATA_DIR=

# Recipient recorded on new-submission notifications.
# RISE_NOTIFY_EMAIL=

# Password for the admin views. The admin area is disabled when unset.
# Use a high-entropy value (e.g. 32+ random characters): it is the entire
# admin auth surface and the session-signing key is derived from it.
# ADMIN_PASSWORD=
